        <briefdescription>
<para>Tokenizes <computeroutput>command</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>flag</computeroutput> into one argv array. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The <computeroutput>flag</computeroutput> text splits on white space. A span in double quotes stays one argument. The function removes the quote marks and drops empty tokens. The <computeroutput>command</computeroutput> text is not split.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>command</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The toolchain row&apos;s own <computeroutput>command</computeroutput>, placed at argument index zero. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>flag</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The toolchain row&apos;s own <computeroutput>flag</computeroutput>, tokenized after <computeroutput>command</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><computeroutput>command</computeroutput> followed by the arguments of <computeroutput>flag</computeroutput>. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
